\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.4}{\ignorespaces A sketch of the LO and AS beam paths. The LO beam path is shown in blue and the AS beam is shown in red. A dashed line indicates the direction that the recombining beamsplitter, BHDBS2, moves. When this happens, at the point of the beams combining the phase of the AS beam has increased while the phase of the LO beam has decreased. This means that the recombination beamsplitter motion needs to be counted twice.\relax }}{16}{figure.caption.13}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbhddoublecounted}{{1.4}{16}{A sketch of the LO and AS beam paths. The LO beam path is shown in blue and the AS beam is shown in red. A dashed line indicates the direction that the recombining beamsplitter, BHDBS2, moves. When this happens, at the point of the beams combining the phase of the AS beam has increased while the phase of the LO beam has decreased. This means that the recombination beamsplitter motion needs to be counted twice.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.5}{\ignorespaces The phase noise between the LO and the AS beams causes noise. The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve is shown in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the requirement of HRTS mirror motion.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.14}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterhrtsrequirement}{{1.5}{17}{The phase noise between the LO and the AS beams causes noise. The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve is shown in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the requirement of HRTS mirror motion.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
